System Hardening Checklist
System Description: macOS
Checklist
Enable latest updates- this will protect the system from security vulnerabilities 
Configure firewall- when surfing the internet, it's important for the user to be protected from common exploits such as SQL injections
Strong authentication- Making sure the user has a password that's not vulnerable to brute-force attacks
Disable unused services- If the app isn't a default app (such as Maps) that the user doesn't use, the user must take precautions to delete any unnecessary applications
Configure backups- it's imperative for the user to have backups in case theyy lose their primary file or their system is exposed to vulnerabilities 
